      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city boasts more than 200 historic buildings, including eight National Register listings, preserving its 19th‑century industrial heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cedarburg.org/visitor-center/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1939, Carl Kiekhaefer founded Mercury Marine in Cedarburg, launching a company that would become a global marine engine leader.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedarburg%2C_Wisconsin",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Cedarburg History Museum, housed in the historic Hilgen & Schroeder Mill Store, serves as the town’s visitor center and preserves local lore.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedarburg%2C_Wisconsin",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cedar Creek powered early lumber, flour, and nail mills, a brewery, and later a railroad that arrived in 1870, spurring rapid growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cedarburg.org/visitor-center/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A local legend tells of a tractor driver who once crossed a county bridge with a snowplow, only to reverse and splash back, highlighting quirky town lore.",
